    "narrative": "The Austin Waves lineup today is headlined by **Gunnar Henderson**, who registers an elite efficiency score of 83.29. Facing Hancock, **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from a massive 16% park adjustment and a 14% platoon edge, making him the clear focal point of our offensive production. While **Gunnar Henderson** has a slight penalty for Hancock's ability to limit stolen bases, his elevated spot in the order (+8%) and raw power potential keep him firmly in the top slot for today\u2019s 5x5 objectives. We are also looking for significant output from **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (60.35) and **Miguel Andujar** (67.29), both of whom benefit from favorable matchups against starters with high xERA projections; **Miguel Andujar** specifically capitalizes on a 19% SP skill advantage against Abbott, helping offset his placement in the lower third of the order.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench today was **Nasim Nunez**, who finished with a 44.31 score. While **Nasim Nunez** brings the elite sprint speed we covet for our SB category, his projected #8 spot in the lineup and the difficulty of running against a high-end catcher like the one facing the Webb matchup pushed him just below the threshold required to displace **Coby Mayo** or **Curtis Mead**. We continue to manage our bench carefully with **Kyle Tucker** and **Luis Robert Jr.** remaining unavailable due to rest and injury respectively. Owners should monitor the status of **Curtis Mead**, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, **Miguel Andujar**, **Jackson Merrill**, and **Nolan Schanuel** closely; because their positions are currently \"Lineup Pending,\" any drastic shifts in their projected batting order could compress their efficiency scores and necessitate a late-day swap with reserve options like **Brayan Rocchio**.",
